# Build the inbound ladder tooth

From [Decide the Telegram delivery bar](./decide-telegram-delivery-bar.svx):
the gateway turn-responds to every Slack message Joel sends anywhere, including
channel messages to other humans. Joel told it not to on 2026-07-27 and prose
lost. This step makes the ladder mechanical.

Resolved when:

- The transport stamps every `inbound.received` as `addressed` or `ambient` at
  ingress (`packages/gateway/src/chat-sdk-inbound/`): addressed = Telegram DM,
  Slack DM to the bot, explicit @mention, reply in a gateway-started thread,
  button/reaction on a gateway flow; everything else ambient.
- The plugin server (`prototypes/agent-comms-gateway/claude-plugin/server/`)
  refuses reply/ack outbound correlated to an ambient inbound unless an
  escalation receipt exists saying why ambient became addressed.
- Ambient events still demand a decision receipt (silence stays illegal); an
  `observe`-flavored receipt satisfies it. Check what the server-side verb
  guard in joelclaw-api allows before inventing a verb.
- Tests cover: channel message without mention → ambient, no outbound;
  @mention → addressed; escalation path leaves the receipt.

